# Andela Frontend (React + Vite + TS)

## Stack (from Req. doc Section 3)

- **React 18** with **TypeScript** (strict mode on).
- **Vite** as the build tool.
- **Recharts** for all charts (error rate trend, severity distribution, health trends, incident timeline).
- **TanStack Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`) for server state. Do not roll your own loading/error state.
- **React Router** for navigation between the 5 dashboard pages.
- **Testing**: Vitest + React Testing Library.
- **Linting**: ESLint + Prettier, strict TS.

Styling: keep it boring. Vanilla CSS modules or a single utility CSS file. No multi-framework UI libraries unless explicitly added.

## Pages (from Req. doc Component 13)

The dashboard has exactly five routes:

| Route | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `/` (Overview) | Risk score, active incidents, open alerts, monitored services |
| `/incidents` (Incident Center) | Incident list with severity, status, root cause, confidence |
| `/topology` (Topology View) | Service graph, dependency tree, blast radius |
| `/trends` (Trends Page) | Error rate trend, incident timeline, severity distribution, health trends |
| `/incidents/:id/ai` (AI Analysis) | Classification, root cause, remediation, executive summary, runbook references |

## Recommended project structure

```
frontend/
├── index.html
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
├── vite.config.ts
├── src/
│   ├── main.tsx                         # React entry, QueryClientProvider, Router
│   ├── App.tsx                          # Layout + routes
│   ├── pages/
│   │   ├── OverviewPage.tsx
│   │   ├── IncidentCenterPage.tsx
│   │   ├── TopologyPage.tsx
│   │   ├── TrendsPage.tsx
│   │   └── AIAnalysisPage.tsx
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── overview/                    # RiskScoreGauge, ActiveIncidentsCard, ...
│   │   ├── incidents/                   # IncidentTable, IncidentDetail, ...
│   │   ├── topology/                    # ServiceGraph, BlastRadius, ...
│   │   ├── trends/                      # ErrorRateChart, IncidentTimeline, ...
│   │   ├── analysis/                    # ClassificationPanel, RemediationPanel, RunbookReferences
│   │   └── layout/                      # AppShell, Sidebar, TopBar
│   ├── api/                             # one file per resource: events.ts, incidents.ts, ...
│   ├── hooks/                           # useIncidents, useRiskScore, ...
│   ├── lib/                             # formatters, color scales, severity helpers
│   ├── types/                           # API contract types (mirror Pydantic schemas)
│   └── test/setup.ts                    # Vitest + RTL setup
└── tests/                               # cross-feature integration tests if needed
```

Rules:

- Domain folders (`incidents/`, `topology/`, etc.) hold composed components. Page-level orchestration lives under `src/pages/`.
- `src/api/` is the single boundary that talks to the backend. The rest of the app sees typed promises, not `fetch` calls.
- Types in `src/types/` mirror the backend Pydantic schemas. Treat them as the contract — any drift is a bug.

## Component rules

- **One component per file**, named the same as the file.
- **No default exports** for components — named exports only (easier to refactor).
- **Props are explicit interfaces**, not inline types: `interface IncidentCardProps { ... }`.
- **No `any`**. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- **No business logic in components**. Hooks for data, pure helpers for formatting.
- Component must work without a network if its data is mocked — testability check.

## State

- **Server state**: TanStack Query. Cache key conventions:
  - `["incidents", filters]`
  - `["risk-score"]`
  - `["topology"]`
  - `["events", filters]`
  - `["alerts"]`
- **Local UI state**: `useState`, `useReducer`. No global state for this assessment.
- **Forms**: simple controlled components are sufficient — no complex forms in this project.

## Severity / status formatting

Centralize in `src/lib/severity.ts`:

```ts
export type Severity = "critical" | "high" | "medium" | "low";

export const severityLabel: Record<Severity, string> = {
  critical: "Critical",
  high: "High",
  medium: "Medium",
  low: "Low",
};
```

Use semantic class names (`severity-critical`, `status-open`) so colors live in CSS, not in TS.

## Charts

- One chart per Recharts container. Do not nest three charts in one component.
- Chart components receive prepared data; they do not fetch.
- Tooltip text is i18n-ready: define labels in one place per chart.

## Inspecting the running UI

Use the **Browser MCP** (`.cursor/mcp.json`) to inspect the live dashboard during development:

- Validate that the Overview page renders the risk score gauge.
- Step through Incident Center filters and verify pagination.
- Capture screenshots for the deck (`deck/`).

The Browser MCP is for **inspection and verification**, not for generating components.

## Testing rules (mirrors `andela-testing.mdc`)

- Test behavior, not implementation. No snapshot tests.
- Use `screen.getByRole`, `getByLabelText` over `getByTestId`. Test ids are for the few cases where accessible queries are not enough.
- Mock the API at the `src/api/` layer (or use `msw` if integration is needed). Do not mock `useQuery`.
- A component test should not need to navigate the router unless the test is about the router.

## Anti-patterns

- Putting fetch logic in `useEffect`. Use TanStack Query.
- Inline styles for anything but truly one-off rules.
- A 500-line component. Split it.
- `// eslint-disable-next-line` without a comment explaining why.
- Calling `/api/...` directly from a component — go through `src/api/`.

